  "rationale": "Re-recorded because merging origin/main into w60/daily-relevance produces a content revision neither side was ever recorded at. Main re-recorded this file in #61 at provenance.contentHash 6973d2c55f6d7788bbaa6886e507bbde, against a tree with no daily relevance and no library-legacy primitive; this branch re-recorded it at 947f84e5adc4572932b606e72d2c1e9a, against a tree whose estimator still stratified on cellIndex alone and whose sweep ran 32 runs rather than 64. Neither literal describes the union, and the gate refuses it by name: \"provenance.contentHash is 947f84e5adc4572932b606e72d2c1e9a and the baseline was recorded at 6973d2c55f6d7788bbaa6886e507bbde\". So this number is measured on the merged tree rather than chosen from one side of a conflict. The instrument is main s: 64 runs, 16 replicates round-robin over the eight-strategy pool, the (cellIndex, arm) estimator, one gated line per (metric, arm). toleranceK is unchanged at 3, no --tolerance-k was passed, and no tolerance was edited by hand.\n\nThe deltas were measured, not assumed, by running the superseded baseline against the merged tree first -- 64 runs, 1308 s on four contended workers. Of its 90 gated lines, 40 moved by exactly zero, 46 moved inside tolerance, and four exceeded it. All four are the same finding seen from four angles, and three of the four name one strategy:\n\n  referenceNodesGainedFinalQuarter@portal-rush   6.25000 -> 0.750000   -5.50000  (-6.22 SE, tol 2.65165)\n  referenceNodesGainedFinalQuarter (sweep level) 5.03125 -> 4.23438    -0.796875 (-5.32 SE, tol 0.449609)\n  referenceNodesGained@portal-rush              54.7500 -> 51.6250     -3.12500  (-4.29 SE, tol 2.18661)\n  referenceNodesKnown@portal-rush               57.2500 -> 54.1250     -3.12500  (-4.29 SE, tol 2.18661)\n\nUnder portal-rush the universe now very nearly stops finding new nodes in its final quarter -- 6.25 down to 0.75, an 88 percent fall -- and that one arm is large enough to drag the sweep-level mean over its own tolerance as well. The direction is the mechanism this branch adds, acting where it would be expected to act hardest. Daily relevance scales worship yield by how relevant a cell is, so the god s favor income now depends on which cells the universe actually uses; portal-rush is the arm that spends its edicts on portals rather than on widening the ruleset, so it is the arm whose cells go least relevant, and it is the arm whose late discovery collapses. referenceNodesGainedFinalQuarter is precisely the metric the README says exists to tell a universe that is still learning from one that has stopped, and under this one strategy it now says stopped.\n\nThat is recorded here rather than tuned away. Every magnitude involved ships untuned, this file makes no balance claim, and a mechanic that changes the favor economy is supposed to move a gate that plays god verbs. What it must not do is move it silently, which is why the four lines are named above with their standard errors.\n\nNothing else moved far. Every other sweep-level mean stayed inside 1.7 standard errors: referenceKnowledgeInstances -120.453 (-1.68 SE), referenceNodesGained -0.515625 (-1.37 SE), referenceNodesKnown -0.515625 (-1.37 SE), referencePopulation -129.063 (-0.32 SE), referencePopulationChange -129.063 (-0.32 SE), referenceLivingMages -1.78125 (-0.21 SE), referenceGrimoires -2.93750 (-0.20 SE), referenceLibraryDepth -0.125000 (-0.07 SE), and referencePeakPopulation 29490 exactly unchanged. No line became newly available or newly unavailable: the three referenceNodesGainedFinalQuarter arm lines that carry no measurement -- archivist, uniform-random-legal, worship-maximizer -- carried none before and carry none now.\n\nThis branch s own earlier note on this file said the ascension gate moved 0.38 SE. That figure was true of the instrument it was taken on and is not comparable to anything above: it came from a 32-run sweep whose tolerances were estimated by the estimator #61 replaced, the one that folded a 294x between-arm spread into what it called noise. The movement did not grow; the gate learned to see it.",
